{"text": " What are credit cards? Monkeys use leaves to pay for bananas. Monkey eat banana. Life good. Monkey want more banana. But doesn't have the leaves to pay for them. So monkey use a leaf card. This card allows monkey to buy bananas now and pay later. Monkey is borrowing leaves from monkey bank. How do credit cards work? When monkey uses leaf card to buy bananas, the monkey bank pays for those bananas. Monkey now owes the bank those leaves. Monkey has around 30 days to pay back the leaves. If monkey pays back the leaves in time, everything is fine. If not, well, we'll talk about that in a minute. How do you get a credit card? First monkey go to the monkey bank. But monkey bank won't give leaf cards to just any monkey. Monkey have to prove they pay for things regularly. They pay back leaves they owe and they pay back on time. All this information goes into one number called a credit score. This is a number monkey banks use to decide how likely you are to pay back your leaves on time. The better monkey's score, the more likely they are to be approved for a leaf card and the more leaves they are allowed to borrow. In the US, a score above 740 is good. A score above 800 is very good. While anything below 580 is not worth eating, I mean not good. Credit limit. But using a leaf card doesn't mean monkey has unlimited leaves. In fact, most beginner cards only let monkey borrow around 1000 leaves. But as monkey bank trust monkey more, they allow more leaves to be borrowed.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.52, "text": " What are credit cards?", "tokens": [50363, 1867, 389, 3884, 4116, 30, 50439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09873670872634019, "compression_ratio": 1.9598214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 0.00852081086486578}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 1.52, "end": 4.16, "text": " Monkeys use leaves to pay for bananas.", "tokens": [50439, 2892, 13083, 779, 5667, 284, 1414, 329, 35484, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0